"A Here-to-There is a migration of people from lands sheltered by one wizard to another's."
"Historically they were fraught, starting wars or ending disasters; now most are loyalty swaps."
"Real moving days kept by tradition are less common, and informally ceremonial."
"Guardians, wizards or knights, stand by the road before sunrise to be invited to protect the way."
"Villagers ask 'The way may be long and dangerous'; guardians pledge to spend their strength."
"At the village meet, families claim guardians and call the village master out to hear their needs."
"Each speaker ends 'and I will hear that answer, too!'; the master agrees and thanks her assistants."
"Family stones, 'fruit of the land' and the master's gifts may not leave until the day itself."
"New houses get liquid blessings, traditionally turned into a home-filling mist by spell."
"On arrival: 'There are houses here where no hearthfires have burned'; 'We have brought wood.'"
"A thunderous afterparty follows, often with communal casting by a professional celebrant."
